Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:44:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Essay gate review fixes (U03)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Block quotes: a ">" line that interrupts a paragraph starts a block quote
  (as react-markdown reads it), and a block quote's attribution line
  ("> — Amos 3:2") stays prose, so its em-dash is caught; a dash
  attribution with a reference counts as the reference beside the quote.
- Rulebook leakage: "steel manufacturing" no longer reads as "steelman";
  "self implication" without the hyphen is caught.
- Links: a link to this site by its full address fails with the path to
  use, so a retired or redirected essay cannot slip through as "external".
- An H1 underlined with "=" fails like "# Title".
- Clearer messages: an unpaired quotation mark suggests a block quote for a
  quotation longer than a paragraph; an off-shelf essay link may also be a
  newer post the gate cannot see.
- essay-text.mjs finds the repo root with fileURLToPath; CRLF paragraph
  breaks split correctly.
- ci.yml: the gate sits beside validate-no-emdash, away from U10's
  insertion after validate-family, so both patches apply without a
  three-way merge; CLAUDE.md lists it in the same place.
- Two new tests cover these edges (16 in the file).

